# {{lb|en|Singapore|colloquial}} One's [[partner]] in a romantic relationship.
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|author=Ordinary People|newsgroup=soc.culture.singapore|url=https://groups.google.com/forum/#!original/soc.culture.singapore/zNl7NYnmt30/GReuTjP_Jm0J
|date=05/27/1997|passage= C'mon lah!! Wake up.. Y R U stupid girls so CHEAP!! Imagine a baby making out with an adult! Want to have '''stead''',.. Go find 1 16yr old rich kid lah!! At for let those men take advantage!! Remember Men CANNOT be Trusted!! Boys maybe can.}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|author=L.Angel|newsgroup=soc.culture.singapore|url= https://groups.google.com/forum/#!msg/soc.culture.singapore/XOcHT0mijXc/zvJD9eMoW3AJ
|date=04/17/1998|passage= I prefer to know a guy better as a friend first before even considering him as a potential '''stead'''.}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|author=L.Angel|newsgroup=soc.culture.singapore|url= https://groups.google.com/forum/#!original/soc.culture.singapore/HBv-y8nyGU0/O0GmFNtMTBsJ
|date=02/13/1999|passage= One of the best dates I had was with his person who did attempt to impress me with expensive gifts or flowers. My date did asked though but I said no because for somebody who's not my '''stead''' and I dun feel there was a need to. }}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|author= Fann Low|newsgroup= soc.culture.singapore|url= https://groups.google.com/forum/#!original/soc.culture.singapore/5qrjVBpgLlw/kMsSBQAS-0oJ
|date=01/30/2004|passage= after 2 week or so I decide to tell her I like her and asked her to be my '''stead'''. But she tell me she had another guy. So we remain as friend.}}

